1234
01:02:33.391 --> 01:02:36.047
<i>(DISTANT SIRENS WAILING)</i>

1235
01:02:41.134 --> 01:02:43.983
I want you to scare the
living shit out of him, Tim.

1236
01:02:46.607 --> 01:02:49.548
Ain't nothin' sketch a motherfucka...

1237
01:02:49.550 --> 01:02:51.436
than cockin' that hammer back.

1238
01:02:51.438 --> 01:02:53.356
You can't point an unloaded
revolver at someone.

1239
01:02:53.358 --> 01:02:55.501
If he sees there's no
bullets in the chamber

1240
01:02:55.503 --> 01:02:56.749
he's gonna know the gun's empty.

1241
01:02:56.751 --> 01:02:58.416
Then we're fucked.

1242
01:03:01.167 --> 01:03:02.640
Then we hit 'em with the Brown Betty.

1243
01:03:06.767 --> 01:03:09.007
<i>(DOOR BELL RINGS)</i>

1244
01:03:10.638 --> 01:03:11.948
Just a minute.

1245
01:03:11.950 --> 01:03:14.829
You stay here.

1246
01:03:14.831 --> 01:03:15.951
Hey, Joe.

1247
01:03:18.990 --> 01:03:20.173
I'm so glad you came. I knew you would.

1248
01:03:20.175 --> 01:03:23.247
I wish you'd called first, but
I won't hold it against you.

1249
01:03:25.006 --> 01:03:28.141
Ron, I haven't been
straight with you, okay?

1250
01:03:28.143 --> 01:03:30.349
There are people in
Chicago who are after me.

1251
01:03:30.351 --> 01:03:31.885
I told them about Frank,
and they lost it...

1252
01:03:31.887 --> 01:03:33.357
and they said they were coming after you.

1253
01:03:33.359 --> 01:03:35.340
What the fuck!

1254
01:03:35.342 --> 01:03:37.773
Ron! Tell this guy right
now how you conned me!

1255
01:03:37.775 --> 01:03:39.116
Christ! You son of a bitch!

1256
01:03:39.118 --> 01:03:40.653
Tell him how you made money off me!

1257
01:03:40.655 --> 01:03:43.341
- Jesus! Fuck you!
- Tell him!

1258
01:03:43.343 --> 01:03:44.620
(WHINING)

1259
01:03:44.622 --> 01:03:47.148
No! No! Put him down! No! Not Kosher! No!

1260
01:03:47.150 --> 01:03:48.237
(COCKS GUN)

1261
01:03:48.239 --> 01:03:49.134
Where's the fucking money!

1262
01:03:49.136 --> 01:03:50.988
In the top drawer of the desk in there!

1263
01:03:50.990 --> 01:03:52.815
Put him down, please! Put him down!

1264
01:03:58.639 --> 01:04:00.780
I really hate to disappoint
you, but this is not the first...

1265
01:04:00.782 --> 01:04:02.990
time I've been tied up
and had a gun in my face.

1266
01:04:04.654 --> 01:04:10.413
You conned me for a bank loan?

1267
01:04:10.415 --> 01:04:14.032
Wait, you think I used Frank to con you?

1268
01:04:16.175 --> 01:04:18.958
I used you to con Frank.

1269
01:04:21.039 --> 01:04:22.924
Wake up.

1270
01:04:22.926 --> 01:04:24.783
It's called a convincer.

1271
01:04:27.855 --> 01:04:28.781
Jesus.

1272
01:04:28.783 --> 01:04:32.428
You know, you really don't scare me at all.

1273
01:04:32.430 --> 01:04:33.517
Joe.

1274
01:04:33.519 --> 01:04:35.149
Listen to me.

1275
01:04:35.151 --> 01:04:36.205
You're a natural.

1276
01:04:36.207 --> 01:04:38.668
You're born for this.

1277
01:04:38.670 --> 01:04:41.036
You're just like me.

1278
01:04:41.038 --> 01:04:42.956
My God, I can teach you so much.

1279
01:04:42.958 --> 01:04:44.268
What did you say?

1280
01:04:44.270 --> 01:04:46.732
It's gonna cost three
million to close Congenco?

1281
01:04:46.734 --> 01:04:48.877
We'll make more than that in a month.

1282
01:04:48.879 --> 01:04:51.053
And we won't have to split
it with fifteen people.

1283
01:04:51.054 --> 01:04:53.325
You want to play in the big leagues?

1284
01:04:53.327 --> 01:04:54.477
Do yourself a favor.

1285
01:04:54.479 --> 01:04:57.613
Put the gun away, and get
on a plane with me tonight...

1286
01:04:57.615 --> 01:04:59.116
and come to New York.

1287
01:04:59.118 --> 01:05:04.845
And start working together
as we should, as partners.

1288
01:05:04.847 --> 01:05:07.116
You want to be partners?

1289
01:05:07.118 --> 01:05:08.976
Of course.

1290
01:05:15.022 --> 01:05:16.014
Put the gun down.

1291
01:05:20.271 --> 01:05:23.469
All right, let's start right now.

1292
01:05:23.471 --> 01:05:26.061
Cut me in on my half of the bank loan.

1293
01:05:26.063 --> 01:05:27.564
Okay.

1294
01:05:27.566 --> 01:05:29.423
Here's the check.

1295
01:05:35.951 --> 01:05:38.797
That was easy. Just ask next time.

1296
01:05:38.799 --> 01:05:41.388
You can untie me now.

1297
01:05:41.390 --> 01:05:43.628
Looks real alright.

1298
01:05:43.630 --> 01:05:46.064
Oh my God.

1299
01:05:50.126 --> 01:05:52.973
Tim! You brought the door man!

1300
01:05:52.975 --> 01:05:57.229
I... I got him his job. You
probably didn't know that.

1301
01:05:57.231 --> 01:05:59.309
I fucking vouched for you with Wolfgang.

1302
01:05:59.311 --> 01:06:02.732
Are you fucking kidding me?
This is like a joke, right?

1303
01:06:02.734 --> 01:06:05.997
Are you really that low life?
You brought the door man?

1304
01:06:05.999 --> 01:06:07.724
Oh, I'm sorry, he's your body guard.

1305
01:06:07.726 --> 01:06:09.676
You know what? Maybe I'm wrong about you.

1306
01:06:09.677 --> 01:06:13.676
Maybe you are just a low life,
two-bit hustler from the valley.

1307
01:06:13.678 --> 01:06:16.140
And what are you? A schwartze on a leash!

1308
01:06:16.142 --> 01:06:18.128
Why don't tell this ape
to get his fucking...

1309
01:06:21.070 --> 01:06:24.813
What the fuck, Tim! You
were supposed to scare him!

1310
01:06:24.815 --> 01:06:26.573
Why are there bullets in the gun!

1311
01:06:26.575 --> 01:06:29.264
We gotta draw a line.

1312
01:06:31.791 --> 01:06:33.292
You were gonna partner with this guy?

1313
01:06:33.294 --> 01:06:36.237
No! I was just saying
that to get the money!

1314
01:06:36.239 --> 01:06:38.700
Oops.

1315
01:06:38.702 --> 01:06:41.839
<i>(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)</i>

1316
01:06:45.646 --> 01:06:47.660
Your father fell in love with a Geisha.

1317
01:06:47.662 --> 01:06:50.860
She was a tea service girl.

1318
01:06:50.862 --> 01:06:51.980
Yeah, it was fun.

1319
01:06:51.982 --> 01:06:53.484
Enough about us.

1320
01:06:53.485 --> 01:06:57.709
Tell us about you and this
boy, who's 45 minutes late.

1321
01:06:57.711 --> 01:07:00.364
He... he's never late.

1322
01:07:00.366 --> 01:07:02.447
Oh, there he is.

1323
01:07:03.662 --> 01:07:05.356
Joe...

1324
01:07:05.357 --> 01:07:07.276
Hi. This is Joe.

1325
01:07:07.278 --> 01:07:08.812
Hey, Joe.

1326
01:07:08.814 --> 01:07:14.029
So sorry I'm late. Traffic...
Los Angeles traffic.

1327
01:07:14.031 --> 01:07:16.304
Happens to the best of us. Right?

1328
01:07:18.287 --> 01:07:21.419
So, Syd tells us that you are in finance?

1329
01:07:21.421 --> 01:07:24.556
Any chance you are related to
the Hunt Brothers out of Dallas?

1330
01:07:24.558 --> 01:07:26.445
I don't think so.

1331
01:07:26.447 --> 01:07:28.972
Well, it is a shame.

1332
01:07:28.974 --> 01:07:30.829
You know I met Nelson
a couple of years ago.

1333
01:07:30.830 --> 01:07:33.036
He is a real character.

1334
01:07:33.038 --> 01:07:35.629
Where're you from, Joe?

1335
01:07:35.630 --> 01:07:36.684
Van Nuys.

1336
01:07:36.685 --> 01:07:40.716
Hmm. Are your parents still there?

1337
01:07:40.718 --> 01:07:42.700
I'm sorry?

1338
01:07:42.701 --> 01:07:44.558
Your parents, are they still in the valley?

1339
01:07:47.663 --> 01:07:50.349
My father is, yeah, yeah. My mother's not.

1340
01:07:50.351 --> 01:07:51.469
She... I don't know where she is.

1341
01:07:51.471 --> 01:07:53.840
She is in Santa Barbara sometimes, maybe.

1342
01:07:55.438 --> 01:07:57.324
Should we order more drinks?

1343
01:07:57.326 --> 01:07:59.819
I could go for another martini.

1344
01:07:59.821 --> 01:08:02.060
How about a bottle of wine?

1345
01:08:02.062 --> 01:08:04.460
Joe, red or white?

1346
01:08:04.462 --> 01:08:08.557
Oh, he doesn't drink. So,
whatever you want, Daddy.

1347
01:08:08.559 --> 01:08:09.901
- Are you in A.A?
- Mom.

1348
01:08:09.903 --> 01:08:13.644
- What?
- He just doesn't drink.

1349
01:08:13.646 --> 01:08:15.247
I really could use some water.

1350
01:08:17.135 --> 01:08:19.087
Here, just drink mine. Joe, here.

1351
01:08:23.887 --> 01:08:26.764
Joe, you have something on your collar.

1352
01:08:26.766 --> 01:08:27.915
- What?
- Momma.

1353
01:08:27.917 --> 01:08:30.703
Your collar? Is that blood?

1354
01:08:33.294 --> 01:08:37.420
Ahh... I was shaving...
and I must have cut myself.

1355
01:08:37.421 --> 01:08:39.596
- Let me see.
- No, it's nothing.

1356
01:08:39.597 --> 01:08:40.909
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. Yeah, everything's...

1357
01:08:40.910 --> 01:08:43.979
What's wrong? Joe, please...

1358
01:08:43.981 --> 01:08:46.988
Hey, Mr. and Mrs. Evans, welcome back.

1359
01:08:46.990 --> 01:08:48.204
Dean, how are you?

1360
01:08:48.206 --> 01:08:49.708
You've been in Europe
for a few months, right?

1361
01:08:49.710 --> 01:08:51.532
We were in Japan. Just got back.

1362
01:08:51.534 --> 01:08:53.740
Hey, Charlie.

1363
01:08:53.741 --> 01:08:56.493
Oh, Charles, how are your parents?

1364
01:08:56.495 --> 01:08:57.804
Are they still traveling?

1365
01:08:57.806 --> 01:09:00.076
Yeah. Yeah, yeah. They're good.

1366
01:09:00.078 --> 01:09:02.255
Excuse me.

1367
01:09:04.367 --> 01:09:06.060
I just remembered I have
a new client meeting.

1368
01:09:06.062 --> 01:09:07.149
What?

1369
01:09:07.151 --> 01:09:09.004
It was such pleasure to
meet you Mr. and Mrs. Evans.

1370
01:09:09.005 --> 01:09:12.911
Joe. Joe. Joe. Joe!

1371
01:09:16.719 --> 01:09:20.811
Client meeting... I completely forgot.

1372
01:09:20.813 --> 01:09:23.788
- I should go.
- Yeah, yeah, no worries.

1373
01:09:23.790 --> 01:09:26.219
I'm sorry, Dad.

1374
01:09:26.221 --> 01:09:29.007
Darling, he is not a keeper.

1375
01:09:34.861 --> 01:09:38.061
Joe! Are you okay?

1376
01:09:38.062 --> 01:09:40.047
Huh?

1377
01:09:44.399 --> 01:09:45.711
What happened?

1378
01:09:49.678 --> 01:09:52.429
It didn't go according to plan.

1379
01:09:52.431 --> 01:09:54.959
You killed him?

1380
01:09:58.639 --> 01:10:01.804
Hey, hey, look at me. Look at me.

1381
01:10:01.806 --> 01:10:07.244
Fuck Ron. He was a snake and
he got what was coming to him.

1382
01:10:07.246 --> 01:10:09.296
You did what you had to do.
You did the right thing, Joe!

1383
01:10:10.863 --> 01:10:13.648
You did what had to be done.

1384
01:10:15.375 --> 01:10:18.285
Fuckin' come here. We
can still cash his check.

1385
01:10:18.287 --> 01:10:21.164
No one knows he's dead.

1386
01:10:21.166 --> 01:10:22.284
You fucking saved us.

1387
01:10:22.286 --> 01:10:23.757
CHARLIE: Hey guys!

1388
01:10:23.759 --> 01:10:26.828
They don't know. No handcuffs, no blood.

1389
01:10:26.830 --> 01:10:28.971
Fucking Ron invested in
Congenco and he went to New York.

1390
01:10:28.973 --> 01:10:30.637
- That's what happened. That's it.
- Okay.

1391
01:10:30.639 --> 01:10:32.460
Right?

1392
01:10:32.462 --> 01:10:34.157
Hey, hey.

1393
01:10:34.159 --> 01:10:35.821
- Dude.
- Where's he going?

1394
01:10:35.823 --> 01:10:37.516
He's gotta go meet this client.
It's a last minute thing.

1395
01:10:37.518 --> 01:10:39.340
He doesn't need me though. We're
gonna go inside and get a drink.

1396
01:10:39.342 --> 01:10:41.003
I'll tell you about it
inside. Come on, let's go in.

1397
01:10:41.005 --> 01:10:42.990
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
We'll see you later, brother.

1398
01:10:45.998 --> 01:10:49.103
<i>(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)</i>

1399
01:11:06.094 --> 01:11:09.003
Hey, you wanna give me a hand here?

1400
01:11:09.005 --> 01:11:10.896
Not really.

1401
01:11:12.589 --> 01:11:14.095
Let 'em go.

1402
01:11:16.878 --> 01:11:18.892
Careful with this stuff.
Don't get creative.

1403
01:11:18.894 --> 01:11:20.780
Just get it on his face.

1404
01:11:20.782 --> 01:11:22.799
(ACID HISSING)

1405
01:11:42.734 --> 01:11:45.263
Syd, you awake?

1406
01:12:01.871 --> 01:12:03.467
DEAN (V.O.): <i>Until
Ron's check cleared...</i>

1407
01:12:03.469 --> 01:12:05.579
<i>we were dead in the</i> water.

1408
01:12:05.581 --> 01:12:07.533
<i>Desperate for cash.</i>

1409
01:12:07.535 --> 01:12:08.909
<i>Investors were starting
to get anxious.</i>

1410
01:12:08.911 --> 01:12:11.628
<i>And they were still expecting
their fifty percent returns.</i>

1411
01:12:11.630 --> 01:12:14.668
The pool has run dry, and we need cash now.

1412
01:12:14.670 --> 01:12:17.836
Once Ron Levin's check clears, we're fine!

1413
01:12:17.838 --> 01:12:20.395
Barely scratches the surface!

1414
01:12:20.397 --> 01:12:22.700
If the BBC craters, every
document from the past year...

1415
01:12:22.702 --> 01:12:25.900
will be under the microscope
of the IRS and the SEC.

1416
01:12:25.902 --> 01:12:29.708
And when they find Ron
Levin's name, the FBI.

1417
01:12:29.710 --> 01:12:31.789
And when that happens? What
do you think they'll do?

1418
01:12:31.791 --> 01:12:33.551
I don't know, Dean. What'll they do?

1419
01:12:35.279 --> 01:12:38.412
Joe, they could arrest you for murder.

1420
01:12:38.414 --> 01:12:42.157
How? They don't have a case.

1421
01:12:42.159 --> 01:12:45.166
Not unless someone
breaks rank and testifies.

1422
01:12:48.302 --> 01:12:50.221
You know me better than anybody, Joe.

1423
01:12:50.222 --> 01:12:52.875
- Come on.
- Yeah.

1424
01:12:52.877 --> 01:12:56.459
You know that. But I can't
speak for everybody else.

1425
01:12:56.461 --> 01:13:00.780
Why do you think they call me "Mean Dean"?

1426
01:13:00.781 --> 01:13:01.644
Why?

1427
01:13:01.646 --> 01:13:03.339
Because you burned down the game room.

1428
01:13:03.341 --> 01:13:04.908
I didn't burn shit!

1429
01:13:04.910 --> 01:13:08.331
Jake Kastner stole those
fireworks and then fucked me...

1430
01:13:08.333 --> 01:13:09.963
in the ass with a Roman candle.

1431
01:13:09.965 --> 01:13:12.269
I was in the game room getting my foos on

1432
01:13:12.271 --> 01:13:15.853
when all of a sudden he busts
in like a fire bug with a Zippo.

1433
01:13:15.855 --> 01:13:18.700
Alarms are ringing, and I'm
like "Mr. Fox, I didn't do shit!"

1434
01:13:18.702 --> 01:13:20.619
But nobody remembers it that way.

1435
01:13:20.621 --> 01:13:23.023
Because he ran back to the
cabin like a little bit...

1436
01:13:24.717 --> 01:13:25.966
Hey.

1437
01:13:27.214 --> 01:13:28.398
Hi.

1438
01:13:36.719 --> 01:13:39.628
He ran back to the cabins
and told everybody...

1439
01:13:39.630 --> 01:13:40.939
that I burned down that room.

1440
01:13:40.941 --> 01:13:43.184
That it was my idea.

1441
01:13:44.814 --> 01:13:46.509
Do you see what I'm saying?

1442
01:13:46.510 --> 01:13:48.396
You know the law as well as I do.

1443
01:13:48.398 --> 01:13:49.515
First one in gets the deal and...

1444
01:13:49.517 --> 01:13:52.620
Everyone else gets the shaft.

1445
01:13:52.622 --> 01:13:56.174
So watch your back. That's all I'm saying.

1446
01:14:12.525 --> 01:14:13.679
Joe.

1447
01:14:16.847 --> 01:14:18.446
Ron Levin's check bounced.

1448
01:14:22.894 --> 01:14:24.043
DEAN (V.O.): <i>That's
when we reached out...</i>

1449
01:14:24.045 --> 01:14:25.195
<i>to Charlie's friend Izzy.</i>

1450
01:14:25.197 --> 01:14:29.005
<i>The Persian Prince from
the Christmas party.</i>

1451
01:14:29.006 --> 01:14:31.340
<i>Izzy wanted into the BBC badly.</i>

1452
01:14:31.342 --> 01:14:33.643
<i>He told us that his father
could get us financing...</i>

1453
01:14:33.645 --> 01:14:35.564
<i>from his filthy,
rich friends in L.A.</i>

1454
01:14:35.566 --> 01:14:37.453
<i>if we did the old man a favor.</i>

1455
01:14:37.455 --> 01:14:39.213
How well do we actually know this guy?

1456
01:14:39.214 --> 01:14:41.132
- Shh.
- He's connected.

1457
01:14:41.134 --> 01:14:43.309
DEAN (V.O.): <i>Izzy said that
his dad was being watched...</i>

1458
01:14:43.311 --> 01:14:45.676
<i>because of what a big
shot he was in Iran.</i>

1459
01:14:45.678 --> 01:14:47.596
His fortune is tied up in foreign accounts.

1460
01:14:47.597 --> 01:14:49.899
But we think with the help
of our friend in L.A...

1461
01:14:49.901 --> 01:14:51.405
we can recover the estate.

1462
01:14:51.407 --> 01:14:52.523
Yeah.

1463
01:14:52.525 --> 01:14:54.381
What is you and I were talking
about is that maybe we can

1464
01:14:54.383 --> 01:14:55.563
find a way to sneak him down south.

1465
01:14:55.565 --> 01:14:58.444
Get my father to Los Angeles, and we...

1466
01:14:58.446 --> 01:15:01.996
guarantee a seven figure
investment into BBC.

1467
01:15:01.997 --> 01:15:05.775
- A million bucks?
- Yeah, at least.

1468
01:15:08.045 --> 01:15:09.740
DEAN (V.O.): <i>A month ago,
we were negotiating...</i>

1469
01:15:09.742 --> 01:15:11.340
<i>a billion dollar merger.</i>

1470
01:15:11.342 --> 01:15:13.259
<i>Now, we were talking
about smuggling...</i>

1471
01:15:13.261 --> 01:15:14.796
<i>an Iranian tyrant in a box.</i>

1472
01:15:14.798 --> 01:15:15.980
- Yo, Charlie.
- Yeah?

1473
01:15:15.982 --> 01:15:18.639
- If you see anything, honk twice.
- You got it.

1474
01:15:26.510 --> 01:15:28.107
Hello, Mr. Samedi.

1475
01:15:28.109 --> 01:15:30.028
Here it is, just like we discussed.

1476
01:15:30.030 --> 01:15:33.419
So no one notices you leaving.

1477
01:15:33.421 --> 01:15:36.558
This is just until we get
you out of San Francisco.

1478
01:15:38.221 --> 01:15:40.652
Dad, this was our idea.

1479
01:15:40.653 --> 01:15:42.703
See? Lots of space. Yeah, it'll be fine.

1480
01:15:44.686 --> 01:15:45.743
What? Papa?

1481
01:15:47.118 --> 01:15:49.227
Izzy, what the fuck is that?

1482
01:15:49.229 --> 01:15:51.116
It's opium, Dean.

1483
01:15:51.118 --> 01:15:52.238
Opium.

1484
01:15:54.511 --> 01:15:56.172
Ismael...

1485
01:15:56.174 --> 01:15:58.219
You expect me to get in there?

1486
01:15:58.221 --> 01:16:00.684
Okay, you do you want to try it?

1487
01:16:00.686 --> 01:16:02.667
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa! Sorry.

1488
01:16:02.669 --> 01:16:06.414
Dad! To kill my one thing!

1489
01:16:07.951 --> 01:16:09.612
FATHER: These boys are
idiots, just like you!

1490
01:16:09.614 --> 01:16:10.639
Unbelievable.

1491
01:16:14.605 --> 01:16:15.598
(YELLING O.S.)

1492
01:16:23.054 --> 01:16:24.044
Well?

1493
01:16:24.046 --> 01:16:26.445
Ah, he's changed his
mind. He doesn't wanna go.

1494
01:16:26.447 --> 01:16:29.099
This little excursion
cost us fifteen grand.

1495
01:16:29.101 --> 01:16:31.019
He is getting in the goddamn trunk.

1496
01:16:31.021 --> 01:16:33.324
I've explained that to him,
Dean. He's not in the mood.

1497
01:16:33.326 --> 01:16:34.507
Oh, so ah... you have explained it to him?

1498
01:16:34.509 --> 01:16:35.723
- Yeah.
- I'm sorry, oh, okay.

1499
01:16:35.725 --> 01:16:36.845
Maybe I need to explain it to him.

1500
01:16:36.846 --> 01:16:39.885
Maybe I should explain it
to him the old fashion way.

1501
01:16:39.887 --> 01:16:41.519
IZZY: Shut the fuck up, Dean, listen...

1502
01:16:43.021 --> 01:16:45.228
(LOUD CRASHING)

1503
01:16:45.229 --> 01:16:47.149
What the hell?

1504
01:16:48.238 --> 01:16:49.807
Oh, god...

1505
01:16:52.045 --> 01:16:53.454
Oh... fuck.

1506
01:16:56.430 --> 01:16:58.444
DEAN (V.O.): <i>That key was
to a safety deposit box...</i>

1507
01:16:58.446 --> 01:17:02.220
<i>in Beverly Hills, it was
the Persian's nest egg.</i>

1508
01:17:02.222 --> 01:17:03.439
Now what?

1509
01:17:05.998 --> 01:17:07.918
Put him in the trunk.

1510
01:17:32.749 --> 01:17:35.787
Relax, if your dad jumps out,
Izzy, Tim and I gonna grab him.

1511
01:17:35.789 --> 01:17:36.939
Okay?

1512
01:17:36.941 --> 01:17:38.606
Hold down the box.

1513
01:17:39.886 --> 01:17:41.262
- Okay, you ready?
- Yeah.

1514
01:17:45.422 --> 01:17:47.119
He looks dead, Joe.

1515
01:17:49.742 --> 01:17:51.500
No, he's got a pulse.

1516
01:17:51.502 --> 01:17:53.516
Your dad ever overdose, Izzy?

1517
01:17:53.518 --> 01:17:54.764
Yeah, once.

1518
01:17:54.766 --> 01:17:57.292
He could be in a coma.

1519
01:17:57.294 --> 01:17:59.211
Hey, Izzy.

1520
01:17:59.213 --> 01:18:01.612
How much is in here?

1521
01:18:01.614 --> 01:18:03.757
Five million.

1522
01:18:03.759 --> 01:18:05.452
In diamonds.

1523
01:18:05.454 --> 01:18:06.923
Shit...

1524
01:18:06.925 --> 01:18:08.780
DEAN (V.O.): <i>Depending
on who you ask...</i>

1525
01:18:08.782 --> 01:18:12.332
<i>will determine how the
next part of story goes.</i>

1526
01:18:12.334 --> 01:18:15.244
<i>Charlie says he was
in he car behind us.</i>

1527
01:18:15.246 --> 01:18:17.166
<i>And I think Izzy said
he wasn't even there.</i>

1528
01:18:20.078 --> 01:18:22.956
<i>And that leaves me versus Joe.</i>

1529
01:18:22.958 --> 01:18:25.646
<i>Four friends with four very
different points of views.</i>

1530
01:18:27.949 --> 01:18:31.563
Syd... hey. I need to talk to you, please.

1531
01:18:31.565 --> 01:18:32.588
Joe, what's wrong?

1532
01:18:32.590 --> 01:18:34.604
Leave town with me. Let
us just go, you and me.

1533
01:18:34.606 --> 01:18:36.364
Okay? We can leave right now.
We can go wherever you want.

1534
01:18:36.366 --> 01:18:37.452
Joe, my show is tonight.

1535
01:18:37.454 --> 01:18:39.948
I know, I'm so happy for
you. I'm going to go home

1536
01:18:39.950 --> 01:18:40.876
and I'll pack up our stuff...

1537
01:18:40.878 --> 01:18:42.092
and we can take off right after the show.

1538
01:18:42.094 --> 01:18:44.684
I don't think you understand,
I can't go anywhere with you!

1539
01:18:44.686 --> 01:18:46.923
Sydney, I'm sorry, I've been
a shitty boyfriend, I know.

1540
01:18:46.925 --> 01:18:48.620
But I love you. And I'm gonna make this...

1541
01:18:48.621 --> 01:18:50.092
You have to let me make this up to you.

1542
01:18:50.094 --> 01:18:52.972
When was the last time we
even had a real conversation?

1543
01:18:52.974 --> 01:18:55.563
Everything's been off! Okay?
I... it's hard for me to explain.

1544
01:18:55.565 --> 01:18:58.124
How can you not see how alone I am?

1545
01:18:58.126 --> 01:19:00.651
I do! It's this town! It's this town.

1546
01:19:00.653 --> 01:19:03.020
They build you up to tear you
down. You're never good enough.

1547
01:19:03.022 --> 01:19:04.619
You know how hard it is to
keep my stories straight?

1548
01:19:04.621 --> 01:19:05.548
What?

1549
01:19:05.549 --> 01:19:06.699
The BBC is full of cash.
The BBC's flushed out.

1550
01:19:06.701 --> 01:19:11.019
Ron Levin's gone to New York.
Ron Levin's gone for good!

1551
01:19:11.021 --> 01:19:12.204
What are you talking about?

1552
01:19:12.206 --> 01:19:13.903
What does that even mean, "Gone
for good?" Where's Ron Levin?

1553
01:19:16.654 --> 01:19:20.683
You know what? I don't wanna know.

1554
01:19:20.685 --> 01:19:22.668
Sydney, please.

1555
01:19:22.670 --> 01:19:23.756
Can you please just give me another shot.

1556
01:19:23.758 --> 01:19:25.483
- I have to go.
- Please? Sydney, I'm sorry.

1557
01:19:25.485 --> 01:19:29.100
- Hey... stay.
- No, don't!

1558
01:19:29.102 --> 01:19:30.447
Don't.

1559
01:19:40.589 --> 01:19:42.284
So where have you been?

1560
01:19:42.286 --> 01:19:43.916
I have people who just
showed up screaming for blood.

1561
01:19:43.918 --> 01:19:45.743
I think it was Scott.

1562
01:19:51.886 --> 01:19:53.419
- Fuck the money.
- What?

1563
01:19:53.421 --> 01:19:54.734
- Fuck the money.
- No!

1564
01:19:56.237 --> 01:19:58.605
I'm want to get outta here. Come on.

1565
01:20:00.621 --> 01:20:05.003
Guys. Guys! Kyle, Scott! Come on, guys.

1566
01:20:05.005 --> 01:20:06.892
- Where are you guys going?
- We're goin' home, dude.

1567
01:20:06.894 --> 01:20:09.803
- BBC's falling apart.
- Falling apart?

1568
01:20:09.805 --> 01:20:10.733
Come on, you guys have no balls!

1569
01:20:10.734 --> 01:20:14.092
No, you have no brains!
And there's no money.

1570
01:20:14.094 --> 01:20:16.845
This is bullshit. Our
Joe is fucking bullshit!

1571
01:20:16.846 --> 01:20:19.339
This thing is ours. This thing is real!

1572
01:20:19.341 --> 01:20:21.996
No, no, this thing is over.

1573
01:20:21.998 --> 01:20:24.239
Come on.

1574
01:20:25.838 --> 01:20:27.535
Look, guys.

1575
01:20:29.453 --> 01:20:30.637
Oh, fuck.

1576
01:20:31.533 --> 01:20:32.557
(DOOR SLAMS)

1577
01:21:25.453 --> 01:21:27.310
Sam?

1578
01:21:32.333 --> 01:21:34.348
Where is Ismael?

1579
01:21:34.350 --> 01:21:35.948
I'm gonna kill him.

1580
01:21:35.950 --> 01:21:37.868
Joe!

1581
01:21:37.870 --> 01:21:40.814
<i>(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)</i>

1582
01:21:48.269 --> 01:21:51.339
I got him, Joe!

1583
01:21:51.341 --> 01:21:52.462
(LOUD THUD)

1584
01:21:54.126 --> 01:21:56.303
Agh!

1585
01:21:59.054 --> 01:22:00.748
Dean, Dean, Dean, are you okay?

1586
01:22:00.750 --> 01:22:03.436
- I'm not...
- It's okay.

1587
01:22:03.438 --> 01:22:04.780
I gotta get some rope and tie this guy up.

1588
01:22:04.782 --> 01:22:06.702
Joe. Don't go!

1589
01:22:17.293 --> 01:22:19.246
Joe!

1590
01:23:02.286 --> 01:23:05.036
We have to turn ourselves in.

1591
01:23:05.038 --> 01:23:07.243
What, are you high?

1592
01:23:07.245 --> 01:23:10.124
Look, he was trying to kill
you. Okay? It's self-defense.

1593
01:23:10.126 --> 01:23:12.078
Yeah, because we kidnapped the guy.

1594
01:23:13.933 --> 01:23:15.659
It was a snake, in the trunk...

1595
01:23:15.661 --> 01:23:16.876
he had a seizure and he broke his neck.

1596
01:23:16.877 --> 01:23:18.507
Nobody's gonna believe that, Joe.

1597
01:23:18.509 --> 01:23:20.844
There's way too much evidence everywhere.

1598
01:23:20.846 --> 01:23:22.860
Alright.

1599
01:23:22.862 --> 01:23:24.523
Okay, how do we spin this?

1600
01:23:24.525 --> 01:23:27.052
We dump the body in the desert.

1601
01:23:27.054 --> 01:23:28.524
We forge that conservatorship.

1602
01:23:28.526 --> 01:23:30.410
Izzy won't care as long
as he gets his money.

1603
01:23:30.412 --> 01:23:33.099
He despised the guy.

1604
01:23:33.101 --> 01:23:36.139
Otherwise this is kidnaping
with aggravated circumstances.

1605
01:23:36.141 --> 01:23:39.596
Forget life without parole.
I'm looking at the gas chamber.

1606
01:23:39.598 --> 01:23:44.268
We're looking at the gas chamber.

1607
01:23:44.270 --> 01:23:46.125
Thanks, man.

1608
01:23:58.285 --> 01:24:00.940
Don't you feel guilty?

1609
01:24:00.941 --> 01:24:04.939
Guilty? For that sack of
shit? Who beat his family?

1610
01:24:04.941 --> 01:24:09.261
Put the screws to his
whole country. Fuck no.

1611
01:24:17.165 --> 01:24:19.467
I need to hold my head up, Dean.

1612
01:24:19.469 --> 01:24:23.084
Instead of looking away in
denial for the rest of my life.

1613
01:24:23.086 --> 01:24:27.755
No, no. Don't you dare
start freezing up on me now.

1614
01:24:27.757 --> 01:24:30.059
Everything I've done,
I've for you, and the BBC.

1615
01:24:30.061 --> 01:24:33.196
You promised me. You said
you would do anything for me

1616
01:24:33.198 --> 01:24:35.115
and you would never let me down.

1617
01:24:35.117 --> 01:24:36.587
Don't you dare start now.

1618
01:24:36.589 --> 01:24:38.573
You are my best friend.

1619
01:24:47.918 --> 01:24:49.101
Okay.

1620
01:24:49.103 --> 01:24:53.355
Dean, go home, take a shower,
pound a bottle of Listerine.

1621
01:24:53.357 --> 01:24:55.596
And meet me at the bank at 8:00 AM, okay?

1622
01:24:55.598 --> 01:24:57.644
Don't tell Izzy what
happened to his father.

1623
01:24:57.646 --> 01:24:59.275
Not until after we get the diamonds.

1624
01:24:59.277 --> 01:25:00.491
Hey, we get those diamonds, Joe.

1625
01:25:00.493 --> 01:25:02.412
We can forget any of this ever happened.

1626
01:25:02.414 --> 01:25:09.802
Dean, we get the diamonds?
I'm paying back those loans.

1627
01:25:09.804 --> 01:25:11.596
And I'm out for good.

1628
01:25:11.598 --> 01:25:13.643
You understand?

1629
01:25:13.645 --> 01:25:17.355
You got it, pal.

1630
01:25:17.357 --> 01:25:19.214
8:00 AM.

1631
01:25:24.204 --> 01:25:26.091
Syd Delicious.

1632
01:25:26.093 --> 01:25:27.883
You look like shit.

1633
01:25:27.885 --> 01:25:30.251
- Wow, nice.
- Where's Joe?

1634
01:25:30.253 --> 01:25:31.819
I don't know, Syd, he's your boyfriend.

1635
01:25:31.821 --> 01:25:32.971
Well, were you with him tonight?

1636
01:25:32.973 --> 01:25:34.731
Seriously? Deal with it yourself.

1637
01:25:34.733 --> 01:25:36.236
What have you guys been doing?

1638
01:25:36.237 --> 01:25:37.675
It's been a really long night, Sydney.

1639
01:25:37.677 --> 01:25:40.750
So either shut the fuck
up or get outta here!

1640
01:25:45.677 --> 01:25:47.690
What, you're moving out?

1641
01:25:47.692 --> 01:25:49.196
Yes.

1642
01:25:49.198 --> 01:25:52.012
Now? In the middle of the night?

1643
01:25:52.014 --> 01:25:54.799
Where's Ron Levin?

1644
01:25:57.133 --> 01:25:59.982
You guys did something to him, didn't you?

1645
01:26:01.901 --> 01:26:03.115
Well, I know that you did.

1646
01:26:03.117 --> 01:26:04.908
And I can promise you
everybody else will too.

1647
01:26:04.910 --> 01:26:06.827
No, I didn't do anything to Ron Levin.

1648
01:26:06.829 --> 01:26:09.164
Did you see Joe today? Hey!

1649
01:26:09.166 --> 01:26:11.468
You know, you wish you could be like Joe.

1650
01:26:11.470 --> 01:26:13.292
But you're nothing like him.

1651
01:26:13.294 --> 01:26:15.372
You are really pushing it, Sydney. Okay?

1652
01:26:15.374 --> 01:26:17.227
You ruined Joe.

1653
01:26:17.229 --> 01:26:19.148
All he ever wanted was to belong.

1654
01:26:19.150 --> 01:26:21.739
And you made him think
he needed a BMW for that.

1655
01:26:21.741 --> 01:26:25.484
Joe, could have been anything in the world!

1656
01:26:25.486 --> 01:26:28.651
And now he is twisted and
he is lost because you...

1657
01:26:28.653 --> 01:26:30.284
fucking ruined him!

1658
01:26:30.286 --> 01:26:31.980
No, Joe was locker fodder until he met me!

1659
01:26:31.982 --> 01:26:37.100
A geek you never would have
spread your fucking legs for.

1660
01:26:37.102 --> 01:26:40.364
Where's Ron Levin? Huh?
What did you do to him?

1661
01:26:40.366 --> 01:26:42.123
What did you do!

1662
01:26:42.125 --> 01:26:45.614
Do you really wanna know?
Do you really wanna know?

1663
01:26:47.981 --> 01:26:49.615
Fuck you!

1664
01:26:54.700 --> 01:26:57.614
<i>(DISTANT SIRENS WAILING)</i>

1665
01:27:19.597 --> 01:27:21.357
Joe?

1666
01:27:24.686 --> 01:27:26.926
Joe, you okay?

1667
01:27:28.845 --> 01:27:30.702
It all got away from me.

1668
01:27:34.093 --> 01:27:35.950
All these little choices.

1669
01:27:41.325 --> 01:27:43.182
Not even my choices.

1670
01:27:49.390 --> 01:27:51.245
I need you to notarize a signature for me.

1671
01:27:57.933 --> 01:28:02.157
Who are Hedayat and Ishmael Samedi?

1672
01:28:05.709 --> 01:28:07.755
You don't want to know.

1673
01:28:07.757 --> 01:28:10.187
I don't want to lie to you, okay?

1674
01:28:10.189 --> 01:28:12.555
Joe...

1675
01:28:12.557 --> 01:28:15.052
...you want me to commit fraud for you?

1676
01:28:15.054 --> 01:28:16.910
Maybe lose my license?

1677
01:28:18.189 --> 01:28:20.045
I'm asking you to save me.

1678
01:28:22.860 --> 01:28:26.539
Look, my father appointed
me conservator of his estate.

1679
01:28:26.541 --> 01:28:27.499
He's in Tehran.

1680
01:28:27.501 --> 01:28:29.771
Apparently so.

1681
01:28:29.773 --> 01:28:32.715
There a few more documents to sign...

1682
01:28:32.717 --> 01:28:35.278
before we grant you access
to the safe deposit box.

1683
01:28:39.565 --> 01:28:41.006
Right this way.

1684
01:28:51.980 --> 01:28:53.453
Are you alright?

1685
01:28:57.645 --> 01:29:00.110
Do you know how many people I've lied to?

1686
01:29:03.501 --> 01:29:05.357
Dad, do you know how many people I've hurt?

1687
01:29:07.085 --> 01:29:10.347
I've taken things from people...

1688
01:29:10.349 --> 01:29:15.695
I will never be able to give back to them.

1689
01:29:20.846 --> 01:29:22.542
Never.

1690
01:29:24.750 --> 01:29:26.318
I don't know how I got here.

1691
01:29:31.469 --> 01:29:33.197
We'll get through this.

1692
01:29:40.045 --> 01:29:43.275
Joe Hunt, you are under arrest
for the charge of murder.

1693
01:29:43.277 --> 01:29:44.875
Don't say anything, Joe.

1694
01:29:44.877 --> 01:29:46.508
I'm getting you a lawyer.

1695
01:29:46.509 --> 01:29:48.298
DEAN (V.O.): <i>With Sydney
asking so many questions...</i>

1696
01:29:48.300 --> 01:29:52.363
<i>about Ron Levin, the cops
were sure to connect the dots.</i>

1697
01:29:52.365 --> 01:29:57.291
<i>From Ron, to Joe, to the Persian...</i>

1698
01:29:57.293 --> 01:30:00.234
<i>to me.</i>

1699
01:30:00.236 --> 01:30:02.573
I tried to talk him out of it.

1700
01:30:05.870 --> 01:30:09.579
But Joe and Tim went
into Ron Levin's house.

1701
01:30:09.581 --> 01:30:11.375
They forced him to sign the check.

1702
01:30:13.740 --> 01:30:15.980
And they killed him.

1703
01:30:15.982 --> 01:30:18.092
DEAN (V.O.): <i>For a guy
who saw all the angles...</i>

1704
01:30:18.094 --> 01:30:21.162
<i>Joe should have seen this
one coming a mile away.</i>

1705
01:30:21.164 --> 01:30:22.891
That's when Joe pitched his plan to me...

1706
01:30:22.893 --> 01:30:26.988
Izzy, Tim and Charlie.

1707
01:30:26.990 --> 01:30:31.371
The Persian sneak was
kidnapping, extortion...

1708
01:30:31.373 --> 01:30:36.110
and murder from the very beginning.

1709
01:30:37.517 --> 01:30:39.501
I didn't kill anyone.

1710
01:30:43.054 --> 01:30:44.974
I tried to save the guy.

1711
01:30:46.958 --> 01:30:47.948
I pulled out a screwdriver...

1712
01:30:47.950 --> 01:30:50.570
and drove holes through
the lid of the trunk.

1713
01:30:50.572 --> 01:30:52.845
So... so that he could get oxygen.

1714
01:30:55.277 --> 01:30:58.126
But when I opened the lid of
the trunk and looked inside...

1715
01:31:04.492 --> 01:31:10.701
Persian was staring back at me
with his eyes all bugged out.

1716
01:31:11.949 --> 01:31:16.942
And he was... he was dead.

1717
01:31:21.357 --> 01:31:23.309
It was Joe.

1718
01:31:24.716 --> 01:31:27.434
It was all Joe.

1719
01:31:27.436 --> 01:31:29.742
DEAN (V.O.): <i>Izzy's father
never made it to L.A.</i>

1720
01:31:32.461 --> 01:31:35.694
Yeah, we both thought so, too, but...

1721
01:31:39.724 --> 01:31:41.774
Kill dog?

1722
01:31:45.805 --> 01:31:47.628
You're free to go, Mr. Karney.

1723
01:31:47.630 --> 01:31:49.482
But the State Attorney General's
office will want to hear...

1724
01:31:49.484 --> 01:31:51.242
that story again in the morning.

1725
